2026-10-11T04:50:52.6865404Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6975217Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6986387Z [0m
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6987059Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6987813Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6988150Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6988920Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6989740Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6990171Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6990569Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6991168Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6991438Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6992411Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6993263Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6993953Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6994494Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6994734Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6995034Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6995492Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6995750Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6996128Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6996255Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6996387Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6996546Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.6996907Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7003568Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7003916Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7004044Z I will:
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7004198Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7004489Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7004930Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7005390Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7005802Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7006090Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7006383Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7007002Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7007495Z    /root
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7019239Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7019926Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7033154Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7033884Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7034165Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7035305Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7035878Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7055502Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7056285Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7067447Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7068206Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7068913Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7069220Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7069489Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7069850Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7070278Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7071018Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7071478Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7071703Z If you would like to
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7072463Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7072745Z 
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7089314Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7089960Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-11T04:50:52.7090119Z 
